hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"295","Concerning the carrying of heads: Abdullah ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Usamah, from Bashir ibn Uqbah, from Abu Nadrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met the enemy and said: Whoever brings a head shall have from Allah whatever he wishes. Two men came with a head and disputed over it, so he awarded it to one of them and said: Wish from Allah whatever you will. He said: I wish a sharp sword with which I fight until I am killed. Abu Dawud said: There are hadiths on this subject from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), none of which is sound."
